NAME=gh
VERSION=2.82.1
DESCRIPTION="GitHub CLI — static Go (CGO_ENABLED=0) build from cli/cli source"
CATEGORY=util
DEPS=
URL=https://github.com/cli/cli/archive/refs/tags/v2.82.1.tar.gz
SHA256=999bdea5c8baf3d03fe0314127c2c393d6c0f7a504a573ad0c107072973af973
MAINTAINER=m3os

# Phase 86e — the GitHub CLI on m3OS. Build knobs (see build_gh in
# xtask/src/port_build.rs):
#   GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64  — m3OS speaks the Linux x86_64 syscall ABI.
#   CGO_ENABLED=0            — no C runtime; pure-Go fully-static binary, the
#                             same binary class as the 86d runtime probe /
#                             static CPython / Clang (m3OS's `ld-musl` has no
#                             real `libc.so`, so a dynamic gh could not run).
#   GOTOOLCHAIN=local        — never auto-download a different toolchain.
#   -trimpath -ldflags='-s -w -X github.com/cli/cli/v2/internal/build.Version=<v>'
#                             — reproducible, stripped, version stamped.
#
# BUILD PROVENANCE (the recorded decision): **built-from-source**, NOT prebuilt.
# We pin the gh SOURCE tarball (URL + SHA-256 above) and compile it with the
# SAME Go toolchain the 86d `go` port pins (go1.24.6, read from
# ports/lang/go/Portfile by build_gh — one place to bump the Go version). That
# keeps the embedded Go runtime byte-for-byte the runtime Phase 86d validated on
# m3OS, minimizing the chance gh trips a syscall the 86d bring-up did not
# implement. Because GOTOOLCHAIN=local refuses to upgrade, gh's go.mod `go`
# directive must be <= the pinned toolchain minor: v2.82.1 is `go 1.24.0` — the
# NEWEST gh that builds with Go 1.24.6 (v2.83.0 jumped to `go 1.25`). To move to
# a newer gh, bump the `go` port's toolchain in lockstep (and the build_gh
# recipe-v key). DEPS is empty: a fully static binary has no runtime package
# dependency, and the Go toolchain is a host-side build input, not an m3OS pkg.
#
# ALTERNATIVE PROVENANCE (documented, not used): the official prebuilt release
# binary `gh_<v>_linux_amd64.tar.gz` is also a CGO_ENABLED=0 pure-Go static
# binary (goreleaser) and would need no Go toolchain — but from-source is what
# consumes the 86d toolchain and lets us stamp internal/build.Version, so it is
# the chosen path (mirrors how build_git notes git's plain-Makefile cross).
#
# gh's module dependencies are NOT vendored in this source tarball; build_gh
# fetches them via GOPROXY during the host build (network, exactly like the `go`
# port's toolchain download). The build is reproducible because gh's committed
# go.sum pins every module hash. A warm pkgcache makes a repeat a zero-compiler
# hit. gh is ~55 MB, so it is gated behind the M3OS_WITH_GH image feature
# (mirroring M3OS_WITH_CLANG) and omitted from default images.
